# CHE MESA Grid Template
#
# This is the clean template for setting up Z x M x P MESA grids for
# chemically homogeneous evolution (CHE) studies. All models follow the
# MESA physics defined in ZdivZsun_template/template/MESA_input_src/.

# =====================================================================
# QUICK START
# =====================================================================
#
# 1. From sse_production/, copy this template to a new physics set:
#      ./cp_grid bb_template_new NN_new_physics
#
# 2. Edit grid.conf (email, partitions, walltimes).
#
# 3. Edit MESA physics in ZdivZsun_template/template/MESA_input_src/:
#      - inlist_both: shared physics (EOS, mixing, winds, stopping)
#      - inlist1: per-model settings (mass, omega placeholders)
#      - src/run_star_extras.f90: custom routines
#    The top-level ./mk_grid compiles MESA_input_src once (star is rebuilt
#    automatically if src/ or make/makefile is newer than star). MESA must
#    be activated (mesa-24031) when running ./mk_grid.
#
# 4. Define your grid axes:
#      - z_div_zsun_grid: metallicities as Z/Zsun (one per line)
#      - z_ignore_grid: Z/Zsun values to skip (counter still increments)
#      - ZdivZsun_template/mass_grid: ZAMS masses in Msun
#      - ZdivZsun_template/period_grid: ZAMS spin periods in days
#
# 5. Generate the metallicity grid:
#      ./mk_grid
#    This creates one L1 folder per active Z. To also generate the
#    M x P subgrid inside each, uncomment lines in mk_grid.
#    Otherwise, run ./mk_grid inside each L1 folder individually.
#
# 6. Generate the full run list and dispatch:
#      ./mk_batch_file     # writes run_grid
#      ./dispatch_grid     # submits Slurm array jobs (cpu-single, one task
#                          # per model, ARRAY_CONCURRENCY limit)
#    Use --dry-run to generate scripts without submitting.
#    Lists above MAX_ARRAY_TASKS are split into submit_grid_partN.slurm;
#    submit part 0, then chain the rest:
#      sbatch chain_submit.slurm --first-wait 0

# =====================================================================
# MAP GRID WORKFLOW (CHE window, main sequence only)
# =====================================================================
#
# A dense M x P grid under map/ that only evolves models through the main
# sequence, to map the CHE window cheaply. Models stop at center h1 <= 1d-6
# or surface he4 >= 0.7, whichever comes first.
#
# - Physics: this set's MESA_input_src inlists with the c12 stopping
#   condition replaced by the h1 one, approx21_cr56.net, and
#   map_run_star_extras.f90 (next to mk_map_grid) as run_star_extras.
# - Build: map/map_template/ gets its own compiled star; map L3 dirs
#   symlink to it (inlist_both links to the per-L1 map copy, inlist1 is real).
# - Grid: full ZdivZsun_template/mass_grid x period_grid for every
#   non-ignored Z in z_div_zsun_grid.
#
# Steps (from the physics-set root, MESA activated):
#
# 1. Create the map grid (writes map/run_grid, map/grid.conf and links to
#    ../dispatch_grid, ../lib, ../z_div_zsun_grid, ../z_ignore_grid):
#      ./mk_map_grid --dry-run      # summary only
#      ./mk_map_grid
#
# 2. Dispatch (no mk_batch_file step; run_grid already exists):
#      cd map
#      ./dispatch_grid [--dry-run]
#    If the list was split into parts, submit part 0 and chain the rest:
#      sbatch chain_submit.slurm --first-wait 0
#
# map/grid.conf takes GRID_EMAIL, MESA_ACTIVATE_CMD, SLURM_PARTITION_SINGLE
# and MAX_ARRAY_TASKS from the parent grid.conf, and sets
# CPUS_PER_TASK=8, ARRAY_WALLTIME=04:00:00, ARRAY_CONCURRENCY=120.
# To rebuild, remove map/ first (mk_map_grid refuses to overwrite it).

# =====================================================================
# SPARSE GRID WORKFLOW
# =====================================================================
#
# Runs only an optimally selected subset of (M, P) points per metallicity.
# select_sparse_grid.py reads an HDF5 of core properties from an already
# run grid, which can be either:
#   (a) a complete grid (e.g. 00_fiducial), or
#   (b) a map grid (see MAP GRID WORKFLOW).
#
# Both HDF5 types are built in the analysis repo
# (/home/hd/hd_hd/hd_lt355/gpfs/hd_lt355-cher/repos/35peak_che) by
# scripts/get_core_properties_v7.py, submitted via Slurm:
#   (a) scripts/get_00_core_props.sh
#       -> data/00_fiducial_core_props_df_v7.h5 (select_sparse_grid.py's
#          default --h5)
#   (b) scripts/get_01_map_core_props.sh (uses --map-grid, reads NN_set/map/)
#       -> e.g. data/01_weakmix_core_props_df_map_v7.h5
#
# 1. Copy the template:
#      cd sse_production/
#      ./cp_grid bb_template_new NN_new_physics
#      cd NN_new_physics
#
# 2. Edit grid.conf and MESA physics as for a full grid (QUICK START
#    steps 2-4 above). For (b), the map grid usually lives in this same set
#    (NN_new_physics/map/) and has already been run and processed.
#
# 3. Generate L1 metallicity folders (also compiles the shared star; MESA
#    activated):
#      ./mk_grid
#
# 4. Write per-L1 mass_grid and period_grid.{mass} override files
#    (pyenv activate cher first):
#      (a) ./select_sparse_grid.py --input-grid-type complete \
#              --fraction 0.3 --plot --verbose
#      (b) ./select_sparse_grid.py --input-grid-type map \
#              --h5 /path/to/NN_..._core_props_df_map_v7.h5 \
#              --fraction 0.3 --plot --verbose
#    --input-grid-type defaults to map, and --h5 defaults to the 00_fiducial
#    file, so pass both explicitly.
#
#    Options:
#      --fraction F          Shared fraction for mass and period axes (required)
#      --fraction-m F        Override mass fraction independently
#      --fraction-p F        Override period fraction independently
#      --h5 PATH             Input HDF5 (default: 00_fiducial_core_props_df_v7.h5)
#      --input-grid-type T   complete | map (default: map). "complete" also
#                            counts case A4 models as crashes
#      --gap-neighbors N     CHE domain fill threshold (default 5)
#      --mono-threshold T    Monotonicity enforcement tolerance in Msun (default 1.0)
#      --on-gaps fill|error  Fill gaps (default), or skip Z bins with gaps and
#                            exit 1 listing them (other Z bins are still written)
#      --dry-run             Analyze without writing files
#      --plot                Write diagnostic PDFs
#      --plot-dir DIR        Plot directory (default ./plots)
#      --verbose             Per-Z details
#
# 5. Remove L1 folders select_sparse_grid.py skipped (no HDF5 data for that
#    Z, printed as "WARNING: No HDF5 data ..."). They still hold the full
#    dense mass_grid/period_grid, so their mk_grid would build the complete
#    M x P grid:
#      for l1 in [0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_ZdivZsun_*; do
#          [ -d "$l1" ] || continue
#          if [ -z "$(find "$l1" -maxdepth 1 -name 'period_grid.[0-9]*' -print -quit)" ]; then
#              rm -rf "$l1"
#          fi
#      done
#    Do NOT re-run the top-level ./mk_grid after step 4: it re-copies the
#    dense grid files into every L1 folder and overwrites the selection.
#
# 6. Generate L2/L3 subgrid in each remaining L1 folder (mk_grid picks up
#    the sparse overrides automatically):
#      for zdir in [0-9][0-9]*_ZdivZsun_*/; do (cd "$zdir" && ./mk_grid); done
#
# 7. Generate run list and dispatch:
#      ./mk_batch_file
#      ./dispatch_grid          # or --dry-run first
#    Split lists: sbatch chain_submit.slurm --first-wait 0

# =====================================================================
# DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
# =====================================================================
#
# Three-level grid hierarchy:
#   L1: {PHYS}{ZZ}_ZdivZsun_{z_suffix}/    one per metallicity
#   L2: {NNN}_m{mass}/                      one per ZAMS mass
#   L3: m{mass}_p{period}_w{omega}/         one per spin period (model)
#
# Template hierarchy:
#   ZdivZsun_template/                      L1 template
#     template/                             L2 template
#       MESA_input_src/                     L3 template (MESA work dir) and
#                                           the set's single compiled star
#
# Thin L3 model dirs (no per-model compilation):
#   inlist1, inlist_both                    real copies (inlist1 patched per model)
#   LOGS/                                   real output dir
#   star, rn, re, submit.sh, re_submit.sh,  symlinks ->
#   inlist, inlist_pgstar,                    ../../../ZdivZsun_template/template/MESA_input_src/
#   history_columns.list, profile_columns.list
#
# To rerun a single model by hand, submit from inside its L3 dir (the job
# runs ./rn or ./re relative to the submit dir):
#   cd <L1>/<L2>/<L3> && sbatch submit.sh      # fresh run
#   cd <L1>/<L2>/<L3> && sbatch re_submit.sh   # restart from latest photo
# No grid script calls submit.sh / re_submit.sh.
# run_grid entries are "(cd L3 ; ./rn) &> L3.log". If you change src/ after
# L3 dirs exist, rebuild once in ZdivZsun_template/template/MESA_input_src
# (./mk) while no jobs are running; every model picks up the new binary.

# =====================================================================
# SCRIPTS
# =====================================================================
#
# --- Grid creation ---
# mk_grid             Generate L1 metallicity folders from z_div_zsun_grid
# cp_model             Copy an L1 template to a new L1 folder
# mk_batch_file        Generate run_grid from the existing L1/L2/L3 tree
# dispatch_grid        Submit Slurm array jobs (auto-splits at 1000 tasks)
# chain_submit.slurm   Submit split parts one after another (--tag grid|missing_grid)
# gen_diff             Diff MESA inputs against a reference template
# clean                Remove all generated L1 trees and artifacts
#
# --- Map grids ---
# mk_map_grid          Build map/ (MS-only dense grid, own compiled star)
# map_run_star_extras.f90  run_star_extras used by map grids
#
# --- Sparse grids ---
# select_sparse_grid.py  Select optimal (M,P) subset per Z from a complete- or
#                        map-grid HDF5; writes per-L1 mass_grid and
#                        period_grid.{mass} overrides
#
# --- Gap-filling and restart ---
# mk_missing_grid      Detect and create missing L3 models
# dispatch_missing_grid Submit run_missing_grid via dispatch_grid (same array logic)
# clean_missing_grid    Undo mk_missing_grid changes
#
# --- Monitoring ---
# check_grid_completion.py   Classify models: COMPLETED/CRASHED/RUNNING/PENDING/STALLED
# grid_outcome_summary.py    Classify by evolution: NON-CHE/MERGER/CHE + milestones
# scan_grid_physics.sh       Verify Z/M/omega in inlists match folder paths
# analyze_runtimes.py        Runtime statistics per Z, M
# clean_history_data_all.py  Deduplicate/repair history.data after restarts
#
# --- Safety ---
# permissions_tracker   Freeze/unfreeze grid dirs with sha256 tamper detection
#
# --- Configuration ---
# grid.conf            Cluster settings (email, partition, walltime, nodes)
#
# --- Shared libraries ---
# lib/common.sh        Shell functions: patch_inline, fortran_d, is_z_ignored,
#                      get_physics_id, load_grid_conf, activate_mesa_snippet
#
# --- Archive ---
# archive/             Older versions of scripts kept for reference

# =====================================================================
# CLUSTER NOTES
# =====================================================================
#
# GPFS does not reliably store Unix exec bits. After git clone or cp_grid,
# scripts may lose +x. Fix with:
#   git update-index --chmod=+x <file>
#   chmod +x <file>
#
# For heavy filesystem scans (check_grid_completion.py on 6720+ models),
# use srun to run on a compute node rather than the login node.
